999       +           Shells.json outputs[id=Out_02] "Demographics and Baseline Characteristics".
1000      +  Population:      ITT Analysis Set (ADSL.ITTFL = 'Y')
1001      +  Column variable: ADSL.TRT01PN (1=Drug A, 2=Drug B, format TRTFMT.)
1002      +  Rows (Label / variable / where-clause / category list, verbatim from the shell JSON):
1003      +     1. Count of Subjects by Treatment  -> table header
1004      +     2. Age (years)                     -> ADSL.AGE, continuous (n/Mean/SD/Median/Q1,Q3/Min,Max)
1005      +     3. Age Group                       -> ADSL.AGEGR1N: 1='< 65 years', 2='>= 65 years'
1006      +     4. Sex at Birth                    -> ADSL.SEX: 'M'='Male', 'F'='Female' (exactly 2 categories -
1007      +                                           no "Unknown" row is defined in the shell, so none is shown)
1008      +     5. Race                            -> ADSL.RACE: exactly 6 categories (AMERICAN INDIAN OR ALASKA
1009      +                                           NATIVE, ASIAN, BLACK, NATIVE HAWAIIAN OR PACIFIC ISLANDER,
1010      +                                           WHITE, OTHER)
1011      +     6. Ethnicity                       -> ADSL.ETHNIC: exactly 2 categories (NOT HISPANIC OR LATINO,
1012      +                                           HISPANIC OR LATINO)
1013      +     7. Weight (kg)                     -> ADSL.BWT, continuous
1014      +     8. Height (cm)                     -> ADSL.BHT, continuous
1015      +     9. Body Mass Index (kg/m^2)        -> ADSL.BBMI, continuous
1016      +
1017      +  Sex/Race/Ethnicity are recoded via the shared format catalog informats/formats (FSEXC./
1018      +  FSEXN., FRACEC./FRACEN., FETHNICC./FETHNICN.) so the real ADSL controlled-terminology values
1019      +  (e.g. RACE='BLACK OR AFRICAN AMERICAN') resolve correctly. SHOWALL=N is used for every
1020      +  categorical row (Age Group/Sex/Race/Ethnicity) so a category with zero observed participants
1021      +  is never printed as a row unless it actually occurs in the ITT population data.
1022      +----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
